{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If you are wise, you are wise for yourself</b> — like the meaning of 'if you are righteous, what do you give Him?'" "<b>ולצת</b> (and if you mock) — it is the opposite of 'חכמת' (you are wise)." "<b>You alone shall bear</b> — its meaning is 'you alone shall bear the iniquity or the punishment,' for it relies on the reader's knowledge, and ולצת is understood [elliptically], like 'וצמית והלכת אל הכלים' (and if you act treacherously, you go to the vessels), whose meaning is 'and if צמית'; so too this."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra reads ולצת as elliptical for 'and if you mock,' paralleling the conditional structure; the comparison is to Malachi 2:12 (וצמית והלכת), which he similarly reads as 'and if you act treacherously.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:44.787112225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}